    {
      "case_id": "ans_014",
      "answer": "Policy HR\u201109 outlines a three\u2011stage grievance process. First, staff should try an informal resolution by raising the issue with their line manager within 15 working days (the manager must acknowledge within 3 days and discuss within 10 days)\u30101\u3011. If the grievance concerns the line manager, it can be raised with the next manager in the reporting line\u30101\u3011. If informal resolution does not work, a formal grievance must be submitted in writing to HR using form HR\u201109a, after which HR acknowledges receipt within 5 working days, convenes a hearing within 20 working days, and issues a written outcome within 10 working days\u30102\u3011. An appeal can be lodged within 10 working days of the outcome and is heard by a manager not previously involved within 20 working days\u30102\u3011.",
      "refused": false,
      "grounded": true,
      "correct": true,
      "citations_valid": true,
      "fact_recall": 1.0,
      "unsupported_claim_rate": 0.0,
